Main mass-derivative lemma:
```lean
theorem hasDerivAt_sum_of_solvesPDE (G : FiniteHeatOperator X) (R : X → ℝ)
    {K : X → X → ℝ → ℝ} {t : ℝ}
    (h : ∀ x, HasDerivAt (fun s : ℝ => K x y s)
      (-(G.laplacian (fun z => K z y t) x) + R x * K x y t) t) :
    HasDerivAt (fun s : ℝ => ∑ x, K x y s) (∑ x, R x * K x y t) t
```
Proof:
```lean
  have hsum := HasDerivAt.sum (𝕜 := ℝ) (F := ℝ) (u := Finset.univ)
      (fun x _ => h x)
  -- derivative: ∑ x, (-(Δ K)_x + R x K x t)
  have hval : (∑ x, (-(G.laplacian (fun z => K z y t) x) + R x * K x y t))
      = ∑ x, R x * K x y t := by
    rw [Finset.sum_add_distrib, Finset.sum_neg_distrib]
    have hzero : ∑ x, G.laplacian (fun z => K z y t) x = 0 := by
      simp only [FiniteHeatOperator.laplacian_apply, Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct]
      -- ∑ x ∑ z L x z * K z y t = ∑ z (∑ x L x z) * K z y t = 0
      rw [Finset.sum_comm]
      simp_rw [← Finset.sum_mul]  -- careful direction
      apply Finset.sum_eq_zero
      intro z _
      have hcol : ∑ x, G.L x z = 0 := by
        rw [← G.conservative z]  -- conservative z : ∑ y, L z y = 0
        exact Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun x _ => G.symmetric_apply x z)
      rw [hcol, zero_mul]
    rw [hzero, neg_zero, zero_add]
  rw [hval] at hsum
  exact hsum
```
Note `HasDerivAt.sum` usage: `HasDerivAt.sum (u := Finset.univ) (fun x _ => ...)` produces `HasDerivAt (fun s => ∑ x ∈ univ, f x s) (∑ x ∈ univ, d x) t`; need to convert `∑ x ∈ univ` to `∑ x`. The existing code does `convert hterm using 1; ext s; rw [Finset.sum_apply]`. Let me mimic.

Actually simpler: note that `∑ x, G.laplacian (fun z => K z y t) x` = `∑ x, ∑ z, G.L x z * K z y t`. Using `Finset.sum_comm` to get `∑ z, ∑ x, G.L x z * K z y t` then `← Finset.sum_mul` gives `∑ z, (∑ x, G.L x z) * K z y t`. Hmm `Finset.sum_mul : ∑ x, f x * a = (∑ x, f x) * a`. So `∑ x, G.L x z * K z y t = (∑ x, G.L x z) * K z y t`.

Let me write it carefully:
```lean
