5. **Positivity for every R**: `exp(sA) = exp(-sc) exp(s(A + c•1))` with A + c•1 entrywise positive; the entries of exp(s • M) for entrywise positive M are positive for s > 0 (all terms of the series are nonneg and the n=1 term is s M x y > 0). ✓ This works because A + c•1 has strictly positive entries; off-diagonal entries are L x y > 0 and diagonal entries are L x x - R x + c > 0 by choice of c. ✓

